    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6550A\n\nSPONSOR: GALLIVAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system as the \"Tec. 5 Edward Enser Memorial Highway\"\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nDesignates the Portion of State route 75 from Langford Road south to\nShirley Road the Town of North Collins, county of Erie, as the \"Tec. 5\nEdward Enser Memorial Highway\"\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends the highway law by adding a new section 344-m, which\nDesignates the Portion of State route 75 from Langford Road south to\nShirley Road the Town of North Collins, county of Erie, as the \"Tec.  5\nEdward Enser Memorial Highway\n\nSection 2: States that the commissioner of transportation shall provide\nfor the installation and maintenance of adequate signing of the state\nhighway systems as designated pursuant to section 1 of this act. The\ndesignation will be for ceremonial purposes only, and the official name\nof the bridge will not be changed as a result of this act.\n\nSection 3: Provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nTec. 5 Edward Enser served his country in the US Army during the Second\nWorld War, and received the Bronze Star, Purple Heart, Presidential Unit\nCitation, Croix de Guerre with Palm Orders, Distinguished Unit Badge,\nEuropean African Middle Eastern Service Medal w/ 8 Battle Stars, Army of\nOccupation Germany, Rhine, Danube Campaign Medals, WWII Victory Medal,\nand Good Conduct Medal.  This legislation is to pay tribute to Tec. 5\nEdward Enser's honorable and heroic service.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
